findings.body:
**Any Claude Review failure blocks the merge, even at the cap.**

The header (lines 19-21) says the workflow avoids failing checks because a failed check leaves the PR UNSTABLE, which PR Auto-Merge never merges, even at the cap. But only the missing-secret and bot-actor cases are handled. Every other failure becomes a failing check on the head:

- an expired `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` or exhausted usage;
- the 15-minute timeout;
- the action rejecting an actor without write permission, e.g. a triage user adding `review:claude`;
- `post_claude_review.py` exiting 1 on malformed output, or a 422 from the reviews API (line 155);
- a same-head run cancelled by `cancel-in-progress`, e.g. `labeled` and `ready_for_review` arriving together. This PR's own ci.yml comment says a cancelled check on the same head reports as a failure.

**Impact:** the PR then never merges until someone reruns the job or pushes. With a dead token, every labelled PR is stuck.

**Fix:** add `continue-on-error: true` (with a `::warning::`) to the Review step and the Post step, so a failed Claude review just means no Claude review and the PR falls back to Copilot or the cap. Also avoid same-head cancellation, e.g. `cancel-in-progress: false` or a concurrency group keyed on the head SHA.
